  "id": "electronics.analog-circuits.diode-circuits",
  "name": "Diode Circuits",
  "level": "process",
  "parent": "electronics.analog-circuits",
  "description": "Design pedagogy for the first active circuits a practitioner builds with a diode: series and shunt clippers, biased clippers, clampers (DC restorers), freewheeling/flyback protection for inductive loads, AM envelope detectors, and voltage multipliers (doubler/tripler). Treats the diode as a piecewise-linear element (open below V_F, ~0.7 V clamp above) and derives every circuit from that single model.",
  "timeline": "Years 20-30",
  "outputs": [
    "diode-circuit-designs"
  ],
